Starting armor is a fedora and a pair of walking shoes.  A Journalist
also wears spectacles (lenses), carries a camera, has a couple of candy
bars in his pocket, and wields a +1 stiletto (not a plain knife).

Forget about the confuse-self attribute, just have him start with 4
potions of booze.  Journalists are also accustomed to long hours of
work with poor wages, and missing meals (or settling for a crumby
counter lunch at the pub), so they should have an intrinsic bonus on
digestive rate EXCEPT for fruit (which they haven't seen since
childhood, and hence which tastes bitter and nourishes them less than
normal).

I'm thinking that a Journalist should have a special sense of what is
going on, where to find the news ... so an Amulet of ESP or perhaps
just an intrinsic of telepathy.

The obituary skill is a good idea ... the Journalist should be able to
discern the race/class/gender of bones ghosts or other human corpses he
encounters.

The Quest artifact would be related to a journalist's exclusive access
to "sources" - insiders who provide him with his stories.  So, it would
be the Little Black Book and it would be a special spellbook of detect
unseen (and that spell would be the special spell for this class).

Starting with a raven as a pet is too different from everyone else.

Starting Strength is average and Constitution is low, but Dexterity and
Intelligence are high.  Wisdom only average, Charisma average.  I'm
thinking that one of Wisdom or Intelligence can be exercised to >18.
Finally, Journalists must be neutral only.

